      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under argon in a glovebox, 1-methoxy-2-methylpropan-2-ol (1a) in n-hexane was added dropwise to a stirred n-hexane solution of Lu[N(SiMe3)2]3. The clear solution was stirred overnight at ambient temperature. Solvent and the produced silylamine were evaporated and the residue was dried under high vacuum (10^-3 Torr) for 5 h to give a white microcrystalline powder. Single crystals were grown by slow evaporation of n-hexane at ambient temperature.",
